  },
  "body": "As is well-known in the web community, mobile performance is everyone's\r\nproblem. This spec change provides a solution. Furthermore, the solution\r\nproperly respects the Extensible Web Manifesto by giving developers a\r\nlow-level building block they can introduce into any part of their app\r\nin order to eliminate or reverse delays.\r\n\r\nThe solution is very simple: setTimeout() and setInterval() now allow\r\ntheir second argument to be negative, thus allowing developers to\r\nexecute code in the past. This will allow them to do any work necessary\r\nbefore the user even asks for it, guaranteeing an instantaneous (or\r\nfaster) response.\r\n\r\nTests: https://github.com/w3c/web-platform-tests/pull/5311",
